<title>AUSTRALIA: NetComm shares soar after merger.</title>
<headline>NetComm shares soar after merger.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in modem maker NetComm Ltd soared by about 33 percent after its announced a merger with fellow modem group Banksia Technologies Pty Ltd.</p>
<p>At 1.30 p.m. (0330 GMT), NetComm shares were 20 cents or 33.33 percent at 80 cents on light volume.</p>
<p>Under the merger terms, Banksia managing director David Stewart would end up as the principal shareholder of the company.</p>
<p>Estimates show that the merged group would have the largest share of Australia's modem market.</p>
<p>-- Kevin Morrison 61-2 9373-1813</p>
</text>
